<title>JAPAN: DKB apologises to shareholders over payoff scandal.</title>
<headline>DKB apologises to shareholders over payoff scandal.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandal-hit Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank Ltd started its annual shareholders' meeting on Friday with apologies for a scandal involving payoffs to corporate racketeers.</p>
<p>Katsuhiko Kondo, the bank's president, who chaired the shareholders' meeting, said the bank apologised for causing trouble to shareholders because bank executives had been arrested.</p>
<p>Explaining the payoff scandal, Kondo told shareholders that the bank still has 7.5 billion yen of loans outstanding to racketeers.</p>
</text>
